+Simulation-only model comparison commands:
+
+```bash
+# Standard all-optical D2NN (the legacy/default CLI remains unchanged)
+uv run python train.py --task classification --dataset mnist --epochs 20 \
+    --optics-preset d2nn2018_thz --size 64 --layers 3 \
+    --rs-backend fft --seed 42 --deterministic
+
+# Hybrid optical front end plus a compact electronic classifier
+uv run python train.py --task classification --dataset mnist --epochs 20 \
+    --model-variant hybrid --optics-preset d2nn2018_thz \
+    --size 64 --layers 3 --rs-backend fft \
+    --hybrid-pool-size 8 --hybrid-hidden-dim 32 --seed 42 --deterministic
+
+# Pure-electronic simulation baseline
+uv run python train.py --task classification --dataset mnist --epochs 20 \
+    --model-variant electronic --electronic-hidden-dim 18 --seed 42 --deterministic
+
+# Perturbation-aware hybrid training with deployment phase quantization
+uv run python train.py --task classification --dataset mnist --epochs 20 \
+    --model-variant hybrid --optics-preset d2nn2018_thz \
+    --size 64 --layers 3 --rs-backend fft \
+    --train-lateral-shift-max-px 0.5 --train-gap-spacing-error-max-m 1e-4 \
+    --train-phase-noise-std-rad 0.05 --train-detector-noise-std-relative 0.01 \
+    --phase-quantization-levels 8 --optical-perturbation-seed 4201 \
+    --detector-noise-seed 4202 \
+    --seed 42 --deterministic
+```
+
+- Stochastic training perturbations are resampled once per training batch from the explicitly seeded sampler.
+- `d2nn2018_thz` is a pure numerical-simulation preset using `0.75 mm` wavelength, `0.4 mm` pixel pitch, and `30 mm` input/inter-layer/output propagation distances. It does not represent measurements from this project.
+- Optical perturbations and detector noise use separate RNG streams, so detector feature count does not change subsequent optical draws.
+- `--train-gap-spacing-error-max-m` models independent inter-layer propagation-gap error; it is not an absolute layer-position displacement model.
+- Detector noise is a synthetic relative additive simulation proxy, not a calibration of any physical detector.
+- Validation and test disable random displacement/noise. If `--phase-quantization-levels` is set, they retain that deployment quantization and are recorded as `quantized_clean`; otherwise they are `clean_continuous`.
+- The existing `gamma` phase-smoothness term regularizes the latent continuous `layer.phase`, not the quantized deployment mask.
+- The electronic baseline rejects optical activations, propagation overrides, and optical/detector perturbations instead of silently ignoring them.
+- Each classification run writes a state-dict checkpoint and JSON manifest containing the CLI/resolved configuration, seeds, split sizes and split-index hashes, model parameter counts, software/runtime environment, best epoch, test metrics, source hashes, and checkpoint SHA-256.
+- These commands measure numerical simulation behavior only. CPU/GPU wall-clock results are not physical edge-device latency or power measurements.
+
+Generate a dataset-independent optical-scale diagnostic with one synthetic sample per class:
+
+```bash
+uv run python diagnose_optical_scale.py --size 64 --layers 3 --batch-size 10 \
+    --presets paper d2nn2018_thz --rs-backend fft \
+    --output optical_scale_64x3_seed42.json
+```
+
+The diagnostic records mean output intensity plus data-loss and full-composite phase-gradient scales. It includes the current detector-logit numerical floor and is not evidence of physical-device efficiency, latency, or power.
+
+### Frozen Robustness Evaluation
+
+Create the evaluation plan before running any method. Omit `--sample-limit` for formal full-test evaluation; a plan with a test-prefix subset is marked as smoke-only evidence.
+
+```bash
+uv run python evaluate_robustness.py create-plan \
+    --reference-checkpoint checkpoints/reference.pth \
+    --output results/robustness_plan.json \
+    --condition-id mixed-noise --draw-count 20 \
+    --optical-seed 42001 --detector-seed 42002 \
+    --lateral-shift-max-px 0.5 \
+    --gap-spacing-error-max-m 1e-4 \
+    --phase-noise-std-rad 0.05 \
+    --detector-noise-std-relative 0.01
+
+uv run python evaluate_robustness.py run \
+    --plan results/robustness_plan.json \
+    --checkpoint checkpoints/model_seed42.pth \
+    --output-dir results/robustness/model_seed42 \
+    --method-id baseline-d2nn --batch-size 64 --device cpu
+```
+
+For the preregistered study, create one shared 14-condition plan directly from the frozen protocol. Do not create separate plans per condition, because cross-method pairing requires one plan identity and one complete condition/draw set.
+
+```bash
+uv run python evaluate_robustness.py create-protocol-plan \
+    --reference-checkpoint ../artifacts/formal_mnist_v1/best_mnist.formal_mnist_v1_baseline_d2nn_seed42.pth \
+    --protocol ../FORMAL_EXPERIMENT_PROTOCOL.json \
+    --output ../results/formal_mnist_v1/robustness_plan.json
+```
+
+Run every compatible D2NN or hybrid checkpoint against the same plan, then summarize all evaluation directories together:
+
+```bash
+uv run python summarize_robustness.py \
+    --evaluations results/robustness/baseline_seed42 \
+                  results/robustness/baseline_seed43 \
+                  results/robustness/baseline_seed44 \
+                  results/robustness/hybrid_seed42 \
+                  results/robustness/hybrid_seed43 \
+                  results/robustness/hybrid_seed44 \
+    --output-dir results/robustness/summary
+```
+
+- One optical perturbation draw is fixed across the complete selected test scope and across compatible methods.
+- Detector-noise tables are deterministic per sample but feature-schema-specific; a D2NN detector tensor is not claimed to be identical to a hybrid pooled-feature tensor.
+- Draws are aggregated within each independently trained model. Cross-method effects are paired by training seed, condition, and draw ID.
+- New v2 draw records store an integer confusion matrix and a reproducible macro-F1 over all score classes, using zero for classes with a zero denominator. The summary reader remains compatible with historical v1 records.
+- The preregistered minimum for a formal comparison is three paired training seeds. One- or two-seed summaries remain descriptive even when a t interval is mathematically available.
+- Output directories must be absent or empty. Predictions, draw metrics, manifests, source hashes, and artifact hashes are written as auditable records.
+- All values are numerical-simulation outputs. CPU timing, when added, must be described only as fixed-environment software simulation overhead.
+
+Evaluate clean classification separately for every formal method, including the electronic baseline. A protocol-bound run rejects subsets, mismatched method variants, training-perturbation mismatches, and runtime settings that differ from the frozen protocol. The timing artifact uses fixed PyTorch CPU threads, warmup passes, and repeated full-loader forwards; it excludes metric aggregation and artifact I/O.
+
+```bash
+uv run python evaluate_clean.py \
+    --checkpoint ../artifacts/formal_mnist_v1/best_mnist.formal_mnist_v1_baseline_d2nn_seed42.pth \
+    --method-id baseline_d2nn \
+    --protocol ../FORMAL_EXPERIMENT_PROTOCOL.json \
+    --output-dir ../results/formal_mnist_v1/clean/baseline_d2nn_seed42 \
+    --batch-size 128 --cpu-threads 1 \
+    --warmup-repeats 1 --measurement-repeats 5
+```
+
+The clean evaluator writes per-sample predictions, aggregate accuracy, macro-F1, mean cross-entropy, and a CPU software-timing record. Timing repeats improve runtime precision only; they are not independent experimental replicates. The training seed remains the statistical unit. Electronic checkpoints are never submitted to the optical robustness plan.
+
+After all methods and seeds have clean artifacts, summarize them independently from optical robustness results:
+
+```bash
+uv run python summarize_clean.py \
+    --evaluations ../results/formal_mnist_v1/clean/baseline_d2nn_seed42 \
+                  ../results/formal_mnist_v1/clean/baseline_d2nn_seed43 \
+                  ../results/formal_mnist_v1/clean/baseline_d2nn_seed44 \
+                  ../results/formal_mnist_v1/clean/electronic_seed42 \
+                  ../results/formal_mnist_v1/clean/electronic_seed43 \
+                  ../results/formal_mnist_v1/clean/electronic_seed44 \
+    --output-dir ../results/formal_mnist_v1/clean_summary
+```
+
+The summary loader verifies every artifact hash, reconstructs the confusion matrix from per-sample predictions, recomputes macro-F1, and recomputes timing medians and IQRs from raw repeats before any cross-seed aggregation.
